Contents: cargo-c tag source, release Cargo.lock, .cargo/config.toml and 410
vendored crate directories selected by `cargo vendor --locked --versioned-dirs`.
The .cargo/config.toml points at the vendor directory relative to itself
(directory = "vendor"); rebuilding needs nothing but this archive. Proved on
2026-09-24: extract, unpack the tag source beside it, copy Cargo.lock in, and
`cargo metadata --locked --offline --no-deps` succeeds with the network off.
The archive is deterministic: sorted paths, uid/gid 0, numeric owner, fixed
mtime 1970-01-01 UTC, modes normalized (u+rw,go+rX,go-w), then xz -9e with
one thread. Two generations produced the same SHA256.
